Hello all,

I have encountered these issues now with using dartTAG data provided by dart. So far I've always simply adjusted the headers in the data sheets to match the dartseq/cap format, and therefore the labels that dartR is used to.
It's also pretty straight forward to use the different options like "lastmetric" etc. when reading in the dart file. However, it's always a bit tedious and I was wondering if there is anything in the pipeline to streamline this better while DArT pushes out "new" data such as TAG? E.g. would it be possible to implement an option when reading the dart data in to say e.g. "type=TAG" or "SEQ" or "CAP"? and that that then can read the headers accordingly to the type?

Cheers
Katrin

