On Sunday, March 27, 2022 at 5:06:33 PM UTC-7 luis.m...@gmail.com wrote:
> Hi Alvaro,
>
> - In the developing version of dartR, a list of individuals are shown on the screen if you use verbose >=  2. If you want to save a list of individuals that were filtered out, you can use the R command "setdiff" as shown in the code below.
>
> - you can save the graphs and reports to the temporal directory (tempddir) using the parameter "save2tmp", and list all the files in tempdir using the dunction gl.list.reports() and recovere them using the ffunction gl.print.reports(), as shown below.
>
> library(dartR)
> # installing the devoloping version of dartR
> gl.install.vanilla.dartR(flavour = "dev")
> library(dartR)
> # filtering individuals on call rate
> test <- gl.filter.callrate(platypus.gl <http://platypus.gl>,method = "ind",threshold =0.92)
> # individuals that were filtered out
> ind_filtered <- setdiff(indNames(platypus.gl <http://platypus.gl>), indNames(test))
>
> #saving plot and report to the temporal directory (tempdir) using save2tmp
> test_2 <- gl.report.rdepth(platypus.gl <http://platypus.gl>,save2tmp = TRUE)
>
> # listing files in tempdir
> gl.list.reports()
> # recovering plot
> plot_1 <- gl.print.reports(1)
> # recovering table
> table_1 <- gl.print.reports(2)
>
> Cheers,
> Luis
>
